<th id="S3.T1.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Claude 3.5 Sonnet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>)</cite></th>
<td id="S3.T1.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S3.T1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.00\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.00</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.00\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S3.T1.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S3.T1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.50\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.50</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.50\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S3.T1.5.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">5</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the numbers of input and output text tokens, and let <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>base</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>IPPg</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the numbers of image tokens for the baseline image and the IPPg image (with embedded text), respectively. Let <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{o}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{img}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>img</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{img}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the per-token prices for input text, output text, and image tokens. Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.1. Cost Profiling ‣ 3. Design ‣ Token-Efficient Multimodal Reasoning via Image Prompt Packaging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> summarizes the per-token pricing for each model (as of January 2026); across providers, image tokens are priced identically to input text tokens, i.e., <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{img}}=p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>img</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{img}}=p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To isolate the effect of IPPg on inference cost, we condition on a fixed task prompt and decoding configuration and assume that both methods incur the same text token counts. Specifically, <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}^{\mathrm{baseline}}=n_{i}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>baseline</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>IPPg</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}^{\mathrm{baseline}}=n_{i}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{o}^{\mathrm{baseline}}=n_{o}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>baseline</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>IPPg</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{o}^{\mathrm{baseline}}=n_{o}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so any cost difference arises solely from the image token counts (<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>base</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}</annotation></semantics></math> versus <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>IPPg</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The baseline approach (text + image) incurs cost:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cost}_{\mathrm{baseline}}=p_{i}\,n_{i}+p_{\mathrm{img}}\,n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}+p_{o}\,n_{o}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Cost</mi><mi>baseline</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>img</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>base</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cost}_{\mathrm{baseline}}=p_{i}\,n_{i}+p_{\mathrm{img}}\,n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}+p_{o}\,n_{o}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Our IPPg approach (text embedded in image) incurs cost:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cost}_{\mathrm{IPPg}}=p_{\mathrm{img}}\,n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}+p_{o}\,n_{o}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Cost</mi><mi>IPPg</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>img</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>IPPg</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cost}_{\mathrm{IPPg}}=p_{\mathrm{img}}\,n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}+p_{o}\,n_{o}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta n_{\mathrm{img}}=n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}-n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>IPPg</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>base</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta n_{\mathrm{img}}=n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}-n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the additional image tokens incurred by embedding text into the image. Under the assumption <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{img}}=p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>img</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{img}}=p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, IPPg is strictly cheaper than the baseline if and only if</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta n_{\mathrm{img}}&lt;n_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta n_{\mathrm{img}}&lt;n_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">That is, embedding text into an image saves cost whenever the additional image tokens are fewer than the text tokens eliminated.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">IPPg is cheaper when <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cost}_{\mathrm{IPPg}}&lt;\mathrm{Cost}_{\mathrm{baseline}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Cost</mi><mi>IPPg</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>Cost</mi><mi>baseline</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cost}_{\mathrm{IPPg}}&lt;\mathrm{Cost}_{\mathrm{baseline}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{img}}\,n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}+p_{o}\,n_{o}&lt;p_{i}\,n_{i}+p_{\mathrm{img}}\,n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}+p_{o}\,n_{o}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>img</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>IPPg</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>img</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>base</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{img}}\,n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}+p_{o}\,n_{o}&lt;p_{i}\,n_{i}+p_{\mathrm{img}}\,n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}+p_{o}\,n_{o}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">The output cost <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{o}\,n_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{o}\,n_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> cancels from both sides:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{img}}\,n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}&lt;p_{i}\,n_{i}+p_{\mathrm{img}}\,n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>img</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>IPPg</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>img</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>base</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{img}}\,n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}&lt;p_{i}\,n_{i}+p_{\mathrm{img}}\,n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{img}}=p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>img</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{img}}=p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can factor out <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}&lt;n_{i}+n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>IPPg</mi></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>base</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}&lt;n_{i}+n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p">Rearranging gives <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}-n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}&lt;n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>IPPg</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi><mi>base</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{IPPg}}-n_{\mathrm{img}}^{\mathrm{base}}&lt;n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>; i.e., <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta n_{\mathrm{img}}&lt;n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta n_{\mathrm{img}}&lt;n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">[Cost Savings]
When <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta n_{\mathrm{img}}&lt;n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta n_{\mathrm{img}}&lt;n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the per-query cost savings are:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Savings}=p_{i}\,(n_{i}-\Delta n_{\mathrm{img}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Savings</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Savings}=p_{i}\,(n_{i}-\Delta n_{\mathrm{img}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">[Modal Token Equivalence]
Since <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{img}}=p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>img</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{img}}=p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> across all tested models:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\text{ image token}\equiv 1\text{ input text token}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> image token</mtext></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> input text token</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\text{ image token}\equiv 1\text{ input text token}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">in terms of marginal cost. Output tokens are <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times</annotation></semantics></math> (GPT) or <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times</annotation></semantics></math> (Claude) more expensive than input tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">It is worth noting that for OpenAI models, image tokens are computed via a tile-based formula:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{img}}=T_{\mathrm{base}}+T_{\mathrm{tile}}\cdot\lceil W/512\rceil\cdot\lceil H/512\rceil," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>tile</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{img}}=T_{\mathrm{base}}+T_{\mathrm{tile}}\cdot\lceil W/512\rceil\cdot\lceil H/512\rceil,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{base}}=85" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>85</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{base}}=85</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{tile}}=170" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>tile</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>170</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{tile}}=170</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>)</cite>; for Claude, image tokens scale linearly with pixel area <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>)</cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{img}}=\frac{W\cdot H}{750}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mn>750</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{img}}=\frac{W\cdot H}{750}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">In practice, embedding text into an image often adds minimal pixels (e.g., a text banner), which may not increase the tile count when the rendered image remains within the same post-resize tile grid for OpenAI models. When <math id="S3.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta n_{\mathrm{img}}\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>img</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta n_{\mathrm{img}}\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the full text token cost <math id="S3.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\,n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\,n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is saved.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2. </span>IPPg Pipeline</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To initiate IPPg, we take an image, create minimal necessary whitespace above the image, and inject the text prompt into the whitespace.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">With this approach, we not only remove the consideration of text token billing but also minimize the increase in image tokens. Then, we compare the performance and cost to the baseline approach, which involves sending both prompt and image and thus incurring both text and image token costs.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4. </span>Downstream Tasks</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate IPPg across multiple downstream tasks that span vision-language reasoning, document understanding, and long-context code generation. This diversity helps identify when IPPg is most effective and characterize how its benefits depend on modality balance and model architecture. Across all tasks, we report task-specific accuracy metrics alongside token-based billing cost, enabling a direct cost-performance comparison with standard text-based prompting.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1. </span>FAMMA: Financial Multimodal Question Answering</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">FAMMA is a large-scale multimodal benchmark for conversational financial question answering that requires multi-step numerical and logical reasoning in domain-specific terminology. Each query includes text along with up to seven visual inputs (e.g., tables, charts, and document screenshots), mirroring real-world analyst workflows.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">FAMMA is well suited for evaluating IPPg because prompts are verbose while visual inputs are already central. We compare standard text+image prompting with text-in-image, measuring accuracy and inference cost across models, and report results by question type (multiple-choice vs. open-ended) and language (English vs. non-English) to assess sensitivity to prompt structure and linguistic variation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2. </span>PathVQA: Medical Visual Question Answering</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">PathVQA evaluates question answering over pathology images containing complex biomedical structures and no embedded text. This makes it well suited for testing whether embedding textual prompts into images interferes with visual reasoning. We evaluate IPPg by rendering the question prompt directly into the image and comparing it against standard text prompting. Performance is measured by answer accuracy, while efficiency is assessed using image cost metrics.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3. </span>SROIE: Receipt Understanding and Information Extraction</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">SROIE benchmarks information extraction from scanned receipts, including vendor names, dates, and monetary values. The dataset exhibits high variability in layout, text density, and image quality, reflecting real-world document understanding challenges. We use SROIE to assess whether image-embedded prompts affect field-level extraction accuracy under IPPg. Evaluation focuses on numerical fields (cash and change), reporting exact-match accuracy, parsability, and cost per correct extraction.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4. </span>HumanEval: Python Code Generation</h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">HumanEval is a standard benchmark for Python code generation, consisting of 164 programming tasks with correctness evaluated via unit tests. Although the task is purely text-based, it enables analysis of IPPg without native visual input. We compare standard text prompting to rendering the full problem description as an image. Performance is measured using pass@1 accuracy under single-call and two-call repair settings, along with output token length and total inference cost to assess conciseness and efficiency.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.5. </span>CoSQL with MAC-SQL: Conversational Text-to-SQL</h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CoSQL is a large-scale conversational text-to-SQL dataset spanning multiple domains and complex database schema; it has 3007 questions. We evaluate using the MAC-SQL framework, which decomposes SQL generation into three stages: SELECTOR (table selection), DECOMPOSER (query generation), and REFINER (error correction).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This task is especially well suited for IPPg because schema descriptions are long and token-intensive. We replace text-based schema inputs with image-rendered schemas in the SELECTOR and DECOMPOSER stages, while keeping the REFINER stage text-based. Performance is measured using exact-match execution accuracy, while efficiency is evaluated via per-query cost and agent-level token usage. This setting allows us to isolate where text-as-image encoding yields the largest cost savings.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>Result</h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1. </span>IPPg Application for VQA</h3>

<section id="S5.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.1.1. </span>FAMMA</h4>

